.TH SDL_HasRectIntersectionFloat 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HasRectIntersectionFloat \- Determine whether two rectangles intersect with float precision.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_rect.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_HasRectIntersectionFloat(const SDL_FRect *A, const SDL_FRect *B);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If either pointer is NULL the function will return false\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I A
an
.BR SDL_FRect
structure representing the first rectangle\[char46]
.TP
.I B
an
.BR SDL_FRect
structure representing the second rectangle\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if there is an intersection, false otherwise\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetRectIntersectionFloat (3)
